Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8

Hi Sarah,

Following the milling passes under Condition 12 (Spindle Speed S=1040 rpm, Feed Rate F=50 mm/min, Depth of Cut D=0.45 mm), I inspected the face milling cutter inserts under the optical microscope.

Findings:
- Measured average flank wear land (VB) exceeded 0.38 mm on tooth #2 and #4 (exceeding ISO 3685 tool life criterion of 0.35 mm).
- Z_Load_Cell and X_Load_Cell showed heavy axial thrust force fluctuations with audible chatter harmonics.
- Vib_Table sensor recorded elevated mid-band spectral energy.

Action Taken:
I have indexed the tool insert indices and scheduled replacement of the cemented carbide inserts. Do not restart heavy cuts on D=0.45 mm until new inserts are torqued and zeroed.

